  "body": {
    "id": "thm:rational-component-aligned-output-polynomial-bit-enumeration",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Under the premises of \\(\\texttt{thm:component-aligned-exact-once-output-sensitive-enumeration}\\), suppose every entry of the rational input \\(\\mathcal O_G\\) has binary encoding length at most \\(L_{\\mathrm{bits}}\\).  A fraction-free implementation of \\(\\operatorname{Enum}_G^{\\mathrm{CA}}\\), including exact \\(q\\)-DAG construction and component-aligned common-ancestry computation, has deterministic total bit-operation time and storage polynomial in \\(p\\), \\(m\\), \\(L_{\\mathrm{bits}}\\), \\(2^p\\), \\(N_{\\mathrm{out}}^{\\mathrm{CA}}\\), and the total emitted encoding length.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "O_G",
      "L_bits",
      "Enum_G",
      "p",
      "m",
      "N_out_CA"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:fraction-free-bit-handle",
      "def:immutable-original-row",
      "lem:bareiss-minor-growth",
      "thm:qpath-completion-exactness",
      "thm:rational-output-polynomial-bit-enumeration",
      "thm:component-aligned-exact-once-output-sensitive-enumeration"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Apply the denominator clearing and Bareiss argument of \\(\\texttt{thm:rational-output-polynomial-bit-enumeration}\\) to every principal within-view solve.  It gives canonical determinant-ratio representations of all immutable-row coordinates with height \\(O(p^3L_{\\mathrm{bits}}+p\\log p)\\).  The same argument applies to the direct Schur formula defining each entry of \\(C_A^{ab}\\): its two principal-system solves use \\(\\Sigma^{aa}[A,A]\\) and \\(\\Sigma^{bb}[A,A]\\), both positive definite, and the remaining operations combine only a polynomial number of rational inputs and determinant ratios.  Hence every \\(C_A^{ab}\\) entry has polynomial binary height.  Each score \\(q^{ab}(A,r,t)\\) divides only by \\(C_A^{bb}[r,r]>0\\), as proved in \\(\\texttt{thm:qpath-completion-exactness}\\), and exact zero is decided by cross multiplication of polynomial-height integers.\n\nThe operation counts are those of \\(\\texttt{thm:component-aligned-exact-once-output-sensitive-enumeration}\\).  Canonical row certificates, integer fragment keys, exact support tests, Boolean transitive closure, and all rational arithmetic therefore have polynomial bit cost per operation and polynomial stored height.  Multiplying by the output-sensitive operation and storage counts, and adding the emitted encoding length, proves the result.  Each Schur state and row is computed directly from the input blocks, so no rational expression is recursively substituted through the subset lattice.",
    "justification": "The rational lift also covers direct Schur states, q-score equality, live pruning, tuple output, and subclass ancestry.",
    "gap": "Bareiss control of immutable rows alone does not bound rational q-DAG preprocessing.",
    "consumer": "Exact symbolic component-aligned implementations can advertise output-polynomial total bit complexity.",
